      "pronunciationText": "Find the gradient of y equals two to the x at x equals three. Here the base is two. Copy two to the x, then multiply by the natural log of two. So d y by d x is the natural log of two, times two to the x. At x equals three, two cubed is eight, so the gradient is eight times the natural log of two, about five point five five. For the account, that's eight thousand dollars after thirty years, growing at about five and a half thousand dollars a decade. On the graph, the height is eight, and the gradient is point six nine three times that. If you wrote just two to the x, you'd get eight. That's the slope e to the x has at that height."
